'''''Petrea''''' is a genus of evergreen flowering [[vine]]s native to tropical [[Americas]],<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal|last=Rueda|first=Ricardo M.|date=1994|title=Systematics and Evolution of the Genus Petrea (Verbenaceae)|journal=Annals of the Missouri Botanical Garden|volume=81|issue=4|pages=610–652|doi=10.2307/2399914|jstor=2399914|url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/part/30319 }}</ref> ranging from Florida and northeastern Mexico to Bolivia, Paraguay, and southern Brazil.<ref name = powo/>

The genus was named in honour of [[Robert James Petre, 8th Baron Petre|Robert James Petre]], an English [[Patronage|patron]] of botany.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=287450&isprofile=0&|title=Petrea volubilis - Plant Finder|website=www.missouribotanicalgarden.org|access-date=2019-02-12}}</ref>

